7 | Y = A @ C
  |       ^ inner dimensions differ: N = 4 vs 5
  |     - this is Matrix[3,4] [1]
  |         - this is Matrix[5,2] [1]
  = note: `@` contracts the last axis of the left operand with the first axis of the right one: [m, k] @ [k, n] -> [m, n]
  = note: here [3, *4*] @ [*5*, 2] needs 4 == 5
  = note: `N` was fixed to 4 at line 5 (`Z @ B`)
  = help: check the size variable `N`: every `N` in a module (or, per call, in a function) stands for one size

